    "contract": {
        "name": "AntiSnipeFeeHook",
        "desc": "Multi-tenant DynamicFee hook that charges snipers a decaying, LP-bound fee on the first rounds of a\npool (akita-hooks B5.1).\n\n- Permission: DynamicFee. Points: `AfterInitialize | BeforeSwap | Quote`, plus `AfterAddLiquidity` for\n  `SnipeStartFirstLiquidity`. The hook cannot see its install's points, so a FirstLiquidity pool\n  without `AfterAddLiquidity` (or any pool whose clock is still unstarted) starts the clock at its first\n  BeforeSwap: the start fee and the creator exemption never outlive the first trading round.\n- Each pool is configured once through F6: `HookInstall.initData = encode(SnipeInit)` and\n  `HookInstall.funding \u2265 AntiSnipeFunding()` (the config box MBR). A pool that installs it without\n  `AfterInitialize` is never configured and the hook passes.\n- The fee goes to reserves as an ordinary LP fee (the Vault applies it), never to the creator, so a\n  creator cannot snipe their own launch for free. The protocol share applies.\n- It returns `SetFee` with `max(ctx.feeBps, fee)`: the hook never lowers a fee set earlier in the\n  stack (place it after GatedFeeHook). The Vault separately caps the result at `pool.maxFeeBps`, so a\n  pool using this hook needs `maxFeeBps \u2265 startFeeBps` (LaunchManager sets it).\n- Exemption: `ctx.caller == exempt` at `e == 0` pays the running fee. `exempt` can only be the pool\n  creator (for managed launches, LaunchManager), which already chooses the whole hook stack.\n- Deterministic in `Global.round`, so a quote and a swap in the same group agree.",
        "methods": [
            {
                "name": "create",
                "args": [
                    {
                        "type": "uint64",
                        "name": "dex"
                    }
                ],
                "readonly": false,
                "returns": {
                    "type": "void"
                }
            },
            {
                "name": "akitaDexHook",
                "args": [
                    {
                        "type": "uint64",
                        "name": "dex"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "uint64",
                        "name": "hookIndex"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "(uint64,uint64,uint64,address,address,uint64,uint64,address,uint64,uint64,bool,bool,uint64,uint64,uint64,uint64,uint64,uint64,uint64,uint64,uint64,(byte[16],uint64,uint64,uint64),(byte[16],uint64,uint64,uint64),byte[],byte[])",
                        "name": "ctx"
                    }
                ],
                "readonly": false,
                "returns": {
                    "type": "(uint64,uint64,uint64,uint64)"
                }
            },
            {
                "name": "getConfig",
                "args": [
                    {
                        "type": "uint64",
                        "name": "poolId"
                    }
                ],
                "readonly": true,
                "returns": {
                    "type": "(uint64,uint64,uint64,uint64,uint64,uint64,address)"
                }
            },
            {
                "name": "feeAt",
                "args": [
                    {
                        "type": "uint64",
                        "name": "poolId"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "uint64",
                        "name": "round"
                    }
                ],
                "readonly": true,
                "returns": {
                    "type": "uint64"
                },
                "desc": "The anti-snipe fee of `poolId` at `round` (before `max` with the running fee); 0 if unconfigured"
            }
        ],
